  data: {
    LLM: "Count your Bowers! The Jack of the trump suit (Right) and its same-colored brother (Left) are more powerful than the Ace. If you hold the Joker and both Bowers, you possess the 'The Nuts'â€”you can lead with them to clear all other trumps from the table. Don't bid heavily if you only have high Aces; you can easily be blocked by the Jacks.\n\nThe 'Kitty' Discard: After you win the bid and take the Kitty, you must discard three cards. Don't just discard your lowest cards. If you have only one card of a specific suit (a 'Singleton'), discard it! This allows you to trump that suit the first time it is led, gaining a trick you would have otherwise lost.\n\nMisÃ¨re Defense: If an opponent bids MisÃ¨re, your team must work together to 'Force' them to win a trick. Lead suits where you have many low cards. If you see the MisÃ¨re player stalling on a suit (e.g., they play a 7 when you lead a 4), they are afraid of that suit. Lead it again! Defense against MisÃ¨re is about 'Hand-Squeezing' the bidder until they have no choice but to take a trick.",
    Player: "Count your Bowers! The Jack of the trump suit (Right) and its same-colored brother (Left) are more powerful than the Ace. If you hold the Joker and both Bowers, you possess the 'The Nuts'â€”you can lead with them to clear all other trumps from the table. Don't bid heavily if you only have high Aces; you can easily be blocked by the Jacks.\n\nThe 'Kitty' Discard: After you win the bid and take the Kitty, you must discard three cards. Don't just discard your lowest cards. If you have only one card of a specific suit (a 'Singleton'), discard it! This allows you to trump that suit the first time it is led, gaining a trick you would have otherwise lost.\n\nMisÃ¨re Defense: If an opponent bids MisÃ¨re, your team must work together to 'Force' them to win a trick. Lead suits where you have many low cards. If you see the MisÃ¨re player stalling on a suit (e.g., they play a 7 when you lead a 4), they are afraid of that suit. Lead it again! Defense against MisÃ¨re is about 'Hand-Squeezing' the bidder until they have no choice but to take a trick.",
